      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T13:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we propagate allocation failure to the CREATE_CHILD_SA handler, remove the appended child, and return NO_ADDITIONAL_SAS? The caller currently ignores this return value and sends success without installing the IPsec SAs. I reproduced this under debug ASAN: with 2,048 live children, the next request receives an SA payload while the SAD remains at 4,096 entries.",
